      "title": "Brazil cuts work week to 40 hours in win for Lula ahead of runoff",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/15/brazil-cuts-work-week-to-40-hours-lula-bolsonaro-election-runoff",
      "description": "<p>Congress approves constitutional amendment that bans six-day workweeks, which could affect up to 30 million</p><p>Brazil’s congress has approved a constitutional amendment to shorten the working week to a maximum of 40 hours, a move that could affect 30 million workers and that will hand a political victory to the leftist president Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva ahead of the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/scandal-brazil-court-jair-flavio-bolsonaro-power-election-moraes-lula\">presidential runoff</a> in under two weeks.</p><p>In an attempt to overturn the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/marina-silva-flavio-bolsonaro-the-amazon-brazil-president-far-right\">first-round lead</a> secured by his opponent, far-right senator Flávio Bolsonaro, Lula has strongly championed the amendment, which will give some workers an extra day off each week.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/15/brazil-cuts-work-week-to-40-hours-lula-bolsonaro-election-runoff\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
